                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "quantifiers",
                    "title": "Countable and uncountable: how much, how many, a lot of, too",
                    "explanation": "Los nombres contables se pueden contar y tienen plural: «a coat», «two coats». Los incontables no tienen plural: «money», «milk», «bread», «time», «information».\n\n«How many» va con plural y «How much», con incontables. «How much» también pregunta el precio:\n- «How many coats?»\n- «How much money?»\n- «How much is this coat?» / «How much are these shoes?»\n\n«A lot of» sirve para los dos en frases afirmativas. En negativas y preguntas se usan mucho «much» y «many»:\n- «I don't have much money.»\n\n«Too» + adjetivo significa demasiado. Para pedir otra talla:\n- «It's too big.»\n- «Have you got it in a small?»",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "",
                        "Contables",
                        "Incontables"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "Ejemplos",
                          "coat, pound, shop",
                          "money, milk, bread, time"
                        ],
                        [
                          "Pregunta",
                          "How many coats?",
                          "How much money?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "Afirmativa",
                          "a lot of coats",
                          "a lot of money"
                        ],
                        [
                          "Negativa",
                          "not many coats",
                          "not much money"
                        ],
                        [
                          "Precio",
                          "How much are these jeans?",
                          "How much is this coat?"
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "I don't have a lot of money this month.",
                      "How many coats do you want to try?",
                      "How much is this blue one?",
                      "It's too big. Have you got it in a small?"
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "quantifiers",
                    "title": "all, both, most, none · enough",
                    "explanation": "Para hablar de cantidades de un grupo:\n- «All» (todos): «All the coats are in the sale.»\n- «Most» (la mayoría): «Most shops close at six.»\n- «None» (ninguno): «None of the coats fits me.»\n- «Both» (los dos, de dos cosas): «Both coats are nice.»\n\nCon «of» + «the», «my», «these»…: «all of the coats», «most of my friends», «none of them». Con pronombres siempre va «of»: «both of them», «none of us».\n\n«Enough» (suficiente) va antes del nombre y después del adjetivo:\n- «I haven't got enough money.»\n- «This coat isn't warm enough.»\n\nCompáralo con «too» (demasiado):\n- «It's too big.» (más de lo necesario)\n- «It isn't big enough.» (menos de lo necesario)",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "",
                        "Ejemplo",
                        "En español"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "all",
                          "All the shops are open today.",
                          "todas las tiendas"
                        ],
                        [
                          "most",
                          "Most of my friends live in Bristol.",
                          "la mayoría de mis amigos"
                        ],
                        [
                          "none",
                          "None of these coats is small.",
                          "ninguno de estos abrigos"
                        ],
                        [
                          "both",
                          "Both coats are blue.",
                          "los dos abrigos"
                        ],
                        [
                          "enough + nombre",
                          "We've got enough money for a hot chocolate.",
                          "suficiente dinero"
                        ],
                        [
                          "adjetivo + enough",
                          "This coat isn't warm enough.",
                          "no abriga lo suficiente"
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "Most of the coats are in the sale.",
                      "Both jackets are too big for me.",
                      "None of my coats is warm enough for a Bristol winter.",
                      "Have you got enough money? — Yes, I have."
                    ]
                  }
